  "body": "## What changed\n\n- New module `camcraft_geometry::hole_pattern`. `HolePattern::points()` gives the hole centres of four recipes:\n  - a point list;\n  - a line (start, pitch, count, angle);\n  - a grid (start, X and Y pitch, X and Y count, angle; holes along X first);\n  - a bolt-hole circle (centre, diameter, count, start angle), full or partial (`angular_pitch` or `span`).\n- The coordinates use plain trigonometry: x = cx + r cos a, y = cy + r sin a (Smid, *CNC Programming Handbook*).\n- The module refuses bad numbers by the field name: non-finite values, a count of 0, a pitch or diameter of 0 or less, two holes on the same place, a partial circle that closes on itself, and more than 10,000 holes.\n- New MCP tool `add_hole_pattern` (`crates/app/src/mcp/hole_pattern_tools.rs`). It makes a Drill, Bore or Thread operation on the stock, with no 3D model:\n  - The holes start at `top`. The default is the stock top of the active setup. With no stock and no `top`, the tool refuses by name.\n  - `diameter`, `depth` and `through` set each hole. `params` patches the other fields (cycle, pitch, ...), but not `holes`.\n  - Seed heights that measure from the model measure from the stock. A height stated in `params` still wins.\n  - `spot {tool, depth, name}` adds a spot-drill Drill operation (`cycle: spot`) on the same holes, ahead of the main operation.\n  - The two operations are one undo step (`History::begin_group` / `commit_group`, a `BatchCommand`). Both commands are built and checked before either runs, so a refusal changes nothing.\n  - A hole off the stock footprint is made, with a `warning` that names it.\n- `edit::kind_index` and `edit::patched` are now `pub(super)`, so that the new tool uses the same seed and patch path as `add_operation`.\n- Docs: `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` is regenerated (`camcraft-cli mcp reference`). The MCP guide has a new row for the tool.\n- Decision record: `docs/decisions/3195-hole-patterns.md`.\n\n## Cause\n\nBefore this change, an agent had to type each hole as JSON to drill a pattern without a model. A stock-only Drill operation also failed at generate with \"Top of Part Z (From: model top, offset 0) is unresolved: no model loaded\".\n\n## Tests\n\nPins (all red on unchanged `upstream/main`, green now):\n\n- `crates/geometry/tests/geo2d/hole_pattern.rs` (joins the `geo2d` suite): six tests. They cover each recipe, Smid's six-hole circle at 30 degrees, a partial circle by pitch and by span, and the named refusals. Red before the fix: `unresolved import camcraft_geometry::hole_pattern`.\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp/hole_pattern.rs` (joins the `mcp` suite): six tests. Red before the fix: `unknown tool 'add_hole_pattern'`.\n  - `a_bolt_circle_with_a_spot_drill_is_one_undo_step_and_posts_g81`: spot and drill ops, hole values, one undo and one redo, generate, verify ok, Fanuc post with `G81` at the four circle points.\n  - `a_grid_pecks_with_g83_and_round_trips_the_project_file`: 3 x 2 grid, Auto cycle past 4 x D posts `G83`, then save, open, and the same holes.\n  - `a_tapped_line_after_its_tap_drill_posts_g84`: tap drill, then a `TAP-M6` line with the tap cycle, verify ok, post with `G84`.\n  - `a_line_and_a_point_list_fill_bore_and_thread_holes`: Bore and Thread holes.\n  - `bad_numbers_are_refused_by_name_and_change_nothing`: ten refusals by name with no operation added, and the off-stock warning.\n  - `no_stock_and_no_top_is_refused_by_name`.\n\nMutation checks (each guard removed, the pin run, then the guard restored):\n\n- M1, no stock-height swap: 3 MCP pins red (\"no model loaded\" at generate).\n- M2, no build of the main op again after the spot: the bolt-circle pin is red (the spot posts after the drill).\n- M3, no refusal of `holes` in `params`: `bad_numbers...` is red.\n- M4, no partial-circle full-turn guard: `degenerate_and_non_finite...` is red.\n\nGate on the final head `e152c869a`:\n\n- `cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`: 1015 steps, 0 failed, 0 stalled, 37.9 min. This includes `app suites: example_catalog`, `example_catalog_adaptive`, `example_catalog_edge_work`, `golden_cl`, `solid_law_goldens`, `mcp`, `mcp_doc_drift`, `post suites: script_goldens` and `geometry suites: geo2d`.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-geometry -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Goldens moved\n\nNone. The quick gate ran the catalog and golden suites above. `git diff --stat upstream/main -- \"*.nc\" \"*.cl\" \"examples/catalog/**\"` is empty. The change adds a tool and touches no generator or post.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- The heavy lanes and `cargo xtask gate light` did not run. This is a P6 draft. AGENTS.md \"Heavy lanes at review\" asks for no heavy step on it. The light lane is owed before the PR is flagged ready.\n- No UI form. The Stock/Sketch form that the issue names goes to a follow-up issue, which is linked in a comment below. Done means of #3195 lists no UI.\n- A Sketch of circles as the pattern source is not in this PR. The follow-up issue covers it with the UI form.\n- No screenshots: no UI change.\n\n## Overlaps\n\nThe new files have no overlap. Registry lines in other open PRs touch the same files, but different functions:\n- `crates/app/src/mcp/tools.rs` and `crates/app/src/mcp/mod.rs`: #4302, #4288, #4238, #4438 (module and chain list appends).\n- `crates/app/tests/mcp.rs`: #4316, #4302, #4288, #4238 (test module list).\n- `site/content/guide/automate/mcp.md`: #4438, #4302, #4238 (a different table row).\n\nThe PR that merges second refreshes. `docs/agents/mcp-tools.md` must then be generated again.\n\nTwo new test files join existing directory suites (`geo2d`, `mcp`). No new top-level test binary is added.\n\nEffort: high\n\nChangelog: MCP `add_hole_pattern` makes a Drill, Bore or Thread operation from a point list, a line, a grid, or a full or partial bolt-hole circle, with no 3D model. An optional spot drill comes with it in one undo step.\n\nFixes #3195\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
